    "https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/4243735": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Organic Chemistry",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Organic Chemistry. Wilkes University. Wilkes University's Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry invites applications for a Tenure-Track Assistant Professor of Chemistry specializing in Organic Chemistry, pending final budget approval, to begin in August 2027. The successful candidate will teach courses in the organic chemistry sequence, including lectures and laboratories, as well as additional undergraduate chemistry courses aligned with departmental needs and the candidate's expertise. The current teaching load is 24 formula hours per academic year, equivalent to a 4/4 teaching load. The department values effective, engaging instruction that challenges students academically while supporting their success. Candidates should demonstrate a commitment to undergraduate education, evidence-based teaching practices, and meaningful student mentorship. The successful candidate will also be expected to establish an active, sustainable research program that engages undergraduate students and contributes to scholarly productivity through presentations, publications, and other appropriate professional activities. Research plans should be feasible within a primarily undergraduate institution and demonstrate opportunities for meaningful student participation. Candidates are encouraged to consider the use of existing departmental instrumentation and opportunities for external funding. Additional responsibilities include academic advising, curriculum development, and service to the department, college, and university. Key Responsibilities Teach undergraduate organic chemistry lectures and laboratories, along with additional chemistry courses as assigned. Develop and maintain an active research program that meaningfully involves undergraduate students. Mentor and advise students in their academic and professional Contribute to curriculum development and Participate in departmental, college, and university Minimum Qualifications D. in Chemistry or a closely related field completed by August 2027 Demonstrated commitment to undergraduate teaching and student success Evidence of effective teaching or strong potential for instructional effectiveness Potential to establish a productive research program involving undergraduate students Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching organic chemistry lectures and/or laboratories Experience mentoring undergraduate researchers Ability to teach additional undergraduate chemistry courses Familiarity with evidence-based teaching practices Strong communication, interpersonal, and organizational skills Wilkes University is an independent, comprehensive university dedicated to academic excellence in the liberal arts, sciences, and selected professional programs. The University has approximately 2,000 undergraduate students and over 1,500 full time equivalent students at the graduate and first professional levels. Its institutional focus is on developing strong mentoring relationships with each of its students and contributing vitally to economic development of Northeastern Pennsylvania. The University is located in Wilkes-Barre, Pennsylvania, a revitalized city, located on the scenic Susquehanna River, that provides an affordable cost of living and is within two and one-half hours driving distance of New York City and Philadelphia. To apply, visit: https://www.applicantpro.com/openings/wilkesuniversitycareers/jobs . Please submit: Cover letter describing your interest in the position, the University, and qualifications Curriculum vitae Teaching statement (maximum 2 pages): describe your teaching philosophy, instructional strategies, and approach to supporting student learning in undergraduate chemistry courses. Summary of course evaluations, if available Graduate transcripts Research statement (maximum 6 pages including figures, excluding references): describe a research program appropriate for a primarily undergraduate institution, including proposed research directions, opportunities for meaningful undergraduate student involvement, anticipated resource needs, and potential for scholarly dissemination and external funding. Names and contact information for three professional references The position will remain open until filled, with preference given to applicants who submit all required materials by November 13, 2026. Questions may be directed to Dr. Megan Youmans at megan.youmans@wilkes.edu. Wilkes University is constantly seeking to become a more diverse community and to enhance its capacity to value and capitalize on the cultural richness that diversity brings. The University strongly encourages applications from persons with diverse backgrounds. Wilkes University does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs or activities on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, age, religion, disability, pregnancy, sex/gender, gender identity and/or expression, sexual orientation, marital or family status, military or veteran status, or genetic information. Employment at Wilkes is contingent upon the results of a thorough background screening. PA Act 153 requires that persons working in positions with regular and unsupervised contact with minors complete additional clearances, including FBI fingerprinting and PA criminal and child abuse clearances."
    },
    "https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/4211032": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Sports Management",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Sports Management. Wilkes University. The Jay S. Sidhu School of Business and Leadership at Wilkes University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Sports Management position beginning in August 2027. The position is housed in the Department of Marketing and Sports Management within the College of Business and Engineering. The Sidhu School is accredited by AACSB International. Candidates must hold a Ph.D. in Sports Management or a closely related field. ABD candidates will be considered, but the Ph.D. must be completed by the time of appointment. Prior teaching experience in Sports Management, evidence of scholarly activity, and a demonstrated commitment to student mentorship are preferred. The successful candidate will teach undergraduate and graduate courses in areas such as sports analytics, sports finance, sports psychology, sports law, and other sports-related subjects as needed. Additional responsibilities include maintaining an active scholarly agenda, providing service to the department, school, university, profession, and community, advising and mentoring undergraduate students in the Sports Management program, and supervising internships, field experiences, and related student research. Wilkes University is an independent, comprehensive institution dedicated to academic excellence in the liberal arts, sciences, and select professional programs. The University enrolls approximately 2,000 undergraduate students and more than 3,300 graduate and professional students. Its mission emphasizes strong faculty-student mentoring relationships and active contributions to the economic development of Northeastern Pennsylvania. Wilkes University is located in Wilkes-Barre, Pennsylvania, a revitalized city along the scenic Susquehanna River and within two and a half hours of New York City and Philadelphia. Applicants should submit a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and contact information for three professional references. Applications received by November 15 will receive full consideration. The position will remain open until filled. To apply, please visit: https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/ For specific questions regarding the application, please contact Dr. Anna Ma, Search Committee Chair, at han.ma@wilkes.edu . Wilkes University is constantly seeking to become a more diverse community and enhance its capacity to value and capitalize on diversity's cultural richness. The University strongly encourages applications from persons with diverse backgrounds. Wilkes University does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs or activities on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, age, religion, disability, pregnancy, sex/gender, gender identity and/or expression, sexual orientation, marital or family status, military or veteran status, or genetic information."
    },
    "https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/4228916": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Theatre Design",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Theatre Design. Wilkes University. Wilkes University invites applicants for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of Theatre Design (Scenic and Sound) in the Division of Performing Arts, beginning Fall 2027. The Division offers a BFA in Musical Theatre, a BA in Theatre Arts, and a BFA in Theatre Design and Technology, along with minors in Theatre, Music, and Dance. The successful candidate is responsible for: Designing scenery and sound for the Division's four annual mainstage productions Teaching five courses per year in scenic design, sound design, and other areas of expertise Helping grow and develop the BFA in Theatre Design and Technology, including recruiting and mentoring students Supervising scenic painting, set dressing, and props assistants Leading and taking part in production processes, including technical rehearsals, strikes, and shop work Maintaining an active record of scholarly and creative work Contributing to university service The position works alongside a full-time Technical Director and Assistant Technical Director, who provide production support. An MFA in Theatre Design or a related field is required. The ideal candidate will have prior scenic and sound design experience in both professional and university settings, as well as university-level experience teaching design. Salary is commensurate with qualifications and experience. Wilkes University is an independent, comprehensive university dedicated to academic excellence in the liberal arts, sciences, and selected professional programs. The University has approximately 2,000 students at the undergraduate level and over 1,500 full time equivalent students at the graduate and first professional levels. Its institutional focus is on developing strong mentoring relationships with each of its students and contributing vitally to economic development of Northeastern Pennsylvania. The University is located in Wilkes-Barre, Pennsylvania, a revitalized city that is located on the lovely Susquehanna River and is within two and one-half hours driving distance of New York City and Philadelphia. To apply, visit https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/ . Please be sure to include a cover letter, curriculum vitae, samples of creative work (portfolio or website link), and contact information for three references. Review of applications begins December 1, 2026, and continues until the position is filled. Wilkes University is constantly seeking to become a more diverse community and to enhance its capacity to value and capitalize on the cultural richness that diversity brings. The University strongly encourages applications from persons with diverse backgrounds. Wilkes University does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs or activities on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, age, religion, disability, pregnancy, sex/gender, gender identity and/or expression, sexual orientation, marital or family status, military or veteran status, or genetic information. Employment at Wilkes is contingent upon the results of a thorough background screening. PA Act 153 requires that persons working in positions with regular and unsupervised contact with minors complete additional clearances, including FBI fingerprinting and PA criminal and child abuse clearances."
    },
    "https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/4240688": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Cognitive Psychology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Cognitive Psychology. Wilkes University. The Department of Psychology at Wilkes University invites applications for a TENURE-TRACK ASSISTANT PROFESSOR position in Cognitive Psychology, beginning August 2027. We welcome candidates from a broad range of backgrounds related to cognitive psychology or cognitive neuroscience. The successful candidate will contribute to the continued development of our Psychology and Neuroscience majors and will teach undergraduate courses such as Cognition, Introductory Psychology, and courses within our capstone sequence (e.g., senior seminar in the candidate's area of expertise). The standard teaching load is 12 credits per semester. The Department of Psychology comprises six full-time faculty who are dedicated to student success and excellence in teaching. We seek a candidate who demonstrates a strong commitment to undergraduate education and can provide evidence of teaching effectiveness and scholarly productivity commensurate with experience. The new faculty member will be expected to develop an active research program that incorporates undergraduate students, advise majors, and engage in university and professional service. Preference will be given to candidates who embrace the University's culture of developing undergraduate mentoring relationships. A Ph.D. in Cognitive Psychology or related field is required by the time of appointment. ABD candidates will be considered if degree completion will occur by August, 2026. Salary is commensurate with qualifications and experience. Psychology is the largest major in the College of Arts and Sciences and one of the most popular programs at Wilkes University. The department also houses our Neuroscience major. We have active Psychology and Neuroscience Clubs and a Psi Chi chapter. We highly value undergraduate student-faculty research. Faculty regularly collaborate with students and present their work at regional and national conferences. Application Instructions: Please submit the following: Cover letter Curriculum vitae Summary of course evaluations (if available) Graduate transcripts Research statement Statement addressing teaching interests, teaching philosophy, and diversity Additionally, arrange for three letters of recommendation to be sent directly to: Ms. Jacqueline Kurovsky ( jacqueline.kurovsky@wilkes.edu ), Administrative Assistant for the Division of Behavioral and Social Sciences. Review of applications will begin November 12, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Wilkes University is an independent, comprehensive university dedicated to academic excellence in the liberal arts, sciences, and selected professional programs. The University has approximately 2,000 students at the undergraduate level and over 1,500 full time equivalent students at the graduate and first professional levels. Its institutional focus is on developing strong mentoring relationships with each of its students and contributing vitally to economic development of Northeastern Pennsylvania. The University is located in Wilkes-Barre, Pennsylvania, a revitalized city that is located on the lovely Susquehanna River and is within two and one-half hours driving distance of New York City and Philadelphia. To apply, visit https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/ . Please be sure to include a cover letter, resume or curriculum vitae and three references. Wilkes University is constantly seeking to become a more diverse community and to enhance its capacity to value and capitalize on the cultural richness that diversity brings. The University strongly encourages applications from persons with diverse backgrounds. Wilkes University does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs or activities on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, age, religion, disability, pregnancy, sex/gender, gender identity and/or expression, sexual orientation, marital or family status, military or veteran status, or genetic information. Employment at Wilkes is contingent upon the results of a thorough background screening. PA Act 153 requires that persons working in positions with regular and unsupervised contact with minors complete additional clearances, including FBI fingerprinting and PA criminal and child abuse clearances."
    },
    "https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/4221764": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Electrical Engineering",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, Electrical Engineering. Wilkes University. The Department of Mechanical and Electrical Engineering at Wilkes University invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Electrical Engineering position with a preferred specialization in Power Systems. We seek a collaborative teacher-scholar committed to excellence in undergraduate education, hands-on learning, student mentoring, and faculty-student scholarship. The anticipated start date is Fall 2027. Responsibilities: Teach undergraduate electrical engineering courses and associated laboratory courses Contribute to the delivery and continued development of the Electrical Engineering curriculum Develop and maintain an active program of scholarship and research, with opportunities for undergraduate and graduate student participation Advise and mentor undergraduate students Participate in assessment and continuous improvement activities associated with ABET accreditation Contribute to departmental, college, university, and professional service Collaborate with faculty across engineering and related disciplines Areas of Interest: Applicants from all areas of Electrical Engineering will be considered. Particular consideration will be given to candidates whose expertise complements existing faculty strengths and who can contribute to teaching core undergraduate electrical engineering courses. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to: Electric power systems and smart-grid modernization Power electronics, electric drives, and transportation electrification Renewable-energy integration, energy storage, and microgrids Grid resilience, protection, and cybersecurity Related areas of electrical and computer engineering Candidates who can teach across multiple areas of the undergraduate Electrical Engineering curriculum are especially encouraged to apply. Required Qualifications: A Ph.D. in Electrical Engineering, Electrical and Computer Engineering, or a closely related field by the time of appointment A strong commitment to excellence in undergraduate teaching The ability to teach both lecture and laboratory courses The potential to establish a productive program of scholarly activity appropriate to Wilkes University Effective communication and interpersonal skills Preferred Qualifications: Experience teaching undergraduate electrical engineering courses Ability to teach a broad range of core Electrical Engineering subjects Experience developing or teaching engineering laboratories Research interests that provide meaningful opportunities for undergraduate and graduate participation Industrial or professional engineering experience Interest in interdisciplinary collaboration Experience with externally funded research or demonstrated potential to pursue external funding Familiarity with ABET accreditation and continuous improvement processes Wilkes University is an independent, comprehensive university dedicated to academic excellence in the liberal arts, sciences, and selected professional programs. The University has approximately 2,000 students at the undergraduate level and over 1,500 full-time-equivalent students at the graduate and first-professional levels. Its institutional focus is on developing strong mentoring relationships with each of its students and contributing vitally to the economic development of Northeastern Pennsylvania. The University is located in Wilkes-Barre, Pennsylvania, a revitalized city on the Susquehanna River within two and one-half hours' driving distance of New York City and Philadelphia. The Department of Mechanical and Electrical Engineering, part of the College of Business and Engineering at Wilkes University, offers robust undergraduate and graduate programs with an emphasis on experiential learning and interdisciplinary collaboration. The department supports more than 15 teaching laboratories and four research laboratories, providing a strong environment for high-quality undergraduate education, hands-on laboratory experiences, student mentoring, and applied scholarship. To apply, visit https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/. Please submit the following materials: A cover letter describing interest in the position and relevant qualifications A curriculum vitae A one-page statement of teaching philosophy and interests A two-page statement describing research and scholarly interests, including opportunities for undergraduate and graduate student involvement Contact information for three professional references Any additional materials requested through the Wilkes University application system Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Incomplete applications will not be considered. Wilkes University is constantly seeking to become a more diverse community and to enhance its capacity to value and capitalize on the cultural richness that diversity brings. The University strongly encourages applications from persons with diverse backgrounds. Wilkes University does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs or activities on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, age, religion, disability, pregnancy, sex/gender, gender identity and/or expression, sexual orientation, marital or family status, military or veteran status, or genetic information. Employment at Wilkes is contingent upon the results of a thorough background screening. PA Act 153 requires that persons working in positions with regular and unsupervised contact with minors complete additional clearances, including FBI fingerprinting and PA criminal and child abuse clearances."
