    "https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/4240177": {
      "title": "Director, Clinical Mental Health Counseling Program",
      "description": "Director, Clinical Mental Health Counseling Program. Wilkes University. Wilkes University invites applications for a Clinical Mental Health Counseling Program Director. Reporting to the Dean of the College of Health and Education, the Program Director provides academic and administrative leadership for the Clinical Mental Health Counseling program and supports its continued growth, quality, and accreditation compliance. The Program Director oversees program planning, curriculum development and implementation, program policies, student engagement, and academic assessment. The successful candidate will teach hybrid and online graduate courses; advise graduate counseling students; collaborate with University partners to develop and review student-facing policies and services; and participate in admissions, marketing, and other efforts that support program development and enrollment. A central responsibility of this role is guiding the program's ongoing CACREP accreditation work and ensuring compliance with applicable accreditation standards. The Program Director will also maintain an active record of scholarship, participate in University, College, and program committees, contribute to the counseling profession and community, and provide leadership through effective communication and collaboration. Campus presence and University-funded travel may be required for program needs, including residencies and school retreats. Candidates must hold a doctoral degree in Counselor Education and Supervision, preferably from a CACREP-accredited program. Candidates who are completing their dissertation and have an established timeline to graduate by Fall 2027 will be considered. Applicants must hold active National Certified Counselor (NCC) certification and be eligible for professional counselor licensure in Pennsylvania. The ideal candidate will demonstrate experience teaching at the graduate level, preferably in online or hybrid formats; a comprehensive counseling background and strong professional counselor identity; commitment to CACREP accreditation processes; evidence of scholarship; and service to the University, program, profession, and community. Strong interpersonal, organizational, communication, and leadership skills are essential. Wilkes University is an independent, comprehensive university dedicated to academic excellence in the liberal arts, sciences, and selected professional programs. The University has approximately 2,000 students at the undergraduate level and over 1,500 full time equivalent students at the graduate and first professional levels. Its institutional focus is on developing strong mentoring relationships with each of its students and contributing vitally to economic development of Northeastern Pennsylvania. The University is located in Wilkes-Barre, Pennsylvania, a revitalized city that is located on the lovely Susquehanna River and is within two and one-half hours driving distance of New York City and Philadelphia. To apply, visit Wilkes University Careers . Please be sure to include a cover letter, resume or curriculum vitae and three references. Wilkes University is constantly seeking to become a more diverse community and to enhance its capacity to value and capitalize on the cultural richness that diversity brings. The University strongly encourages applications from persons with diverse backgrounds. Wilkes University does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs or activities on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, age, religion, disability, pregnancy, sex/gender, gender identity and/or expression, sexual orientation, marital or family status, military or veteran status, or genetic information. Employment at Wilkes is contingent upon the results of a thorough background screening. PA Act 153 requires that persons working in positions with regular and unsupervised contact with minors complete additional clearances, including FBI fingerprinting and PA criminal and child abuse clearances."
    },
    "https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/4192823": {
      "title": "Director, Upward Bound Program",
      "description": "Director, Upward Bound Program. Wilkes University. Wilkes University invites applicants for a TRIO Director of the Upward Bound Program in the Department of Office of Academic Success. This is a full-time, 12-month administrative staff position (100% time committed to Upward Bound) reporting to the Associate Dean, Academic Success. The successful candidate is responsible for leading, designing, implementing, administering, and managing all activities of the Upward Bound Program to successfully and consistently ensure achievement of its goal of low-income, first-generation students attaining a college degree. The director ensures compliance with the U.S. Department of Education regulations and university policies, manages all aspects of the program, and is responsible for strategic planning, staff supervision, budget/fiscal management, and student services through the program delivery. A Master's degree is required in Education, Social Services, Counseling, or a related field. The ideal candidate will have four or more years prior experience in educational leadership/educational programming (including design, implementation, and management) working with low-income and first-generation students and their families. Experience with Federal TRIO programs is preferred and demonstrated supervisory experience and fiscal/budgetary management is required. Please be sure to include a cover letter, resume or curriculum vitae and three references including names, titles, full mailing address, telephone numbers and email addresses. Review of applications begins immediately. Wilkes University is constantly seeking to become a more diverse community and to enhance its capacity to value and capitalize on the cultural richness that diversity brings. The University strongly encourages applications from persons with diverse backgrounds. Wilkes University does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs or activities on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, age, religion, disability, pregnancy, sex/gender, gender identity and/or expression, sexual orientation, marital or family status, military or veteran status, or genetic information. Employment at Wilkes is contingent upon the results of a thorough background screening. PA Act 153 requires that persons working in positions with regular and unsupervised contact with minors complete additional clearances, including FBI fingerprinting and PA criminal and child abuse clearances."
    },
    "https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/4188702": {
      "title": "EDGE Coordinator/Learning Specialist",
      "description": "EDGE Coordinator/Learning Specialist. Wilkes University. Wilkes University invites applicants for an EDGE Coordinator/Learning Specialist in the Office of Academic Success (OAS) . Overall, OAS includes programs and services related to first year advising, academic support, disability support services, first generation college students, pre-professional heath advising, ACT 101, EDGE Program, and Upward Bound. OAS is dedicated to providing exemplary services to assist all students to achieve academic and intellectual excellence in the liberal arts, sciences, and professional programs, from their initial transition to college through their progress to post-graduate studies and professional careers. The successful candidate is responsible for assessing student needs and designing individualized plans for student success. The professional in this position will also work with students individually and within small groups to provide instruction in learning enhancement strategies, present workshops, and serve as a resource for the campus community. This will include dedicated time supporting students through the Academic Recovery Program (designed to assist students that are currently on academic probation). This position has a particular emphasis on supporting the EDGE Program; program responsibilities include teaching a career exploration course and coordinating program duties such as monitoring student academic performance, developing academic plans, and coordinating weekly study labs. A Master's Degree in an associated field (e.g. counseling, education, psychology) is required. The ideal candidate will have a minimum of three years counseling and/or teaching experience in an educational environment, preferably at the post-secondary level. Salary is commensurate with qualifications and experience. Wilkes University is an independent, comprehensive university dedicated to academic excellence in the liberal arts, sciences, and selected professional programs. The University has approximately 2,000 students at the undergraduate level and over 1,500 full time equivalent students at the graduate and first professional levels. Its institutional focus is on developing strong mentoring relationships with each of its students and contributing vitally to economic development of Northeastern Pennsylvania. The University is located in Wilkes-Barre, Pennsylvania, a revitalized city that is located on the lovely Susquehanna River and is within two and one-half hours driving distance of New York City and Philadelphia. To apply, visit https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/. Please be sure to include a cover letter, resume or curriculum vitae, and three references. Wilkes University is constantly seeking to become a more diverse community and to enhance its capacity to value and capitalize on the cultural richness that diversity brings. The University strongly encourages applications from persons with diverse backgrounds. Wilkes University does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs or activities on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, age, religion, disability, pregnancy, sex/gender, gender identity and/or expression, sexual orientation, marital or family status, military or veteran status, or genetic information. Employment at Wilkes is contingent upon the results of a thorough background screening. PA Act 153 requires that persons working in positions with regular and unsupervised contact with minors complete additional clearances, including FBI fingerprinting and PA criminal and child abuse clearances."
    },
    "https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/4176730": {
      "title": "Human Resources Director",
      "description": "Human Resources Director. Wilkes University. Wilkes University seeks an accomplished, people-focused HR leader to serve as the Director of Human Resources. The Director of Human Resources is a key partner to University leadership – supporting employees, strengthening the University's culture, and advancing its mission. As a trusted advisor to University partners, the Director will have the opportunity to influence strategy, develop people, strengthen employee engagement, and help build an exceptional workplace. We are looking for a collaborative and thoughtful HR professional who brings sound judgment, strong employee-relations skills, and a genuine commitment to serving people. The ideal candidate is someone who can move comfortably between strategic leadership and hands-on HR, build strong partnerships across the University, and approach complex workplace matters with both confidence and compassion. A bachelor's degree in an appropriate or related field is required. The ideal candidate will have five to eight years of progressively responsible management experience in Human Resources, with prior higher education experience preferred. Salary is commensurate with qualifications and experience. Wilkes University is an independent, comprehensive university dedicated to academic excellence in the liberal arts, sciences, and selected professional programs. The University has approximately 2,000 students at the undergraduate level and over 1,500 full time equivalent students at the graduate and first professional levels. Its institutional focus is on developing strong mentoring relationships with each of its students and contributing vitally to economic development of Northeastern Pennsylvania. The University is located in Wilkes-Barre, Pennsylvania, a revitalized city that is located on the lovely Susquehanna River and is within two and one-half hours driving distance of New York City and Philadelphia. If you are an experienced HR leader looking for an opportunity where your work can have a meaningful impact on an entire university community, we invite you to learn more and apply at visit https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/ . Please be sure to include a cover letter, resume or curriculum vitae and three references. Wilkes University is constantly seeking to become a more diverse community and to enhance its capacity to value and capitalize on the cultural richness that diversity brings. The University strongly encourages applications from persons with diverse backgrounds. Wilkes University does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs or activities on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, age, religion, disability, pregnancy, sex/gender, gender identity and/or expression, sexual orientation, marital or family status, military or veteran status, or genetic information."
    },
    "https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/4244467": {
      "title": "Office Assistant",
      "description": "Office Assistant. Wilkes University. Wilkes University invites applications for an Office Assistant in the College of Business and Engineering. This position supports daily office operations and student engagement across the College, including the Air Force ROTC program. Primary responsibilities include coordinating prospective student and cadet visits, scholarship interviews, recruiting events, and orientations; assisting with student organization activities and departmental events; preparing recruitment materials; and overseeing purchasing of uniforms, equipment, and supplies. The Office Assistant works collaboratively with College staff, faculty, and campus partners to support a positive experience for current and prospective students and cadets. The successful candidate will communicate professionally, respond to inquiries, handle confidential matters with discretion, and maintain positive working relationships across the University. Strong organization, attention to detail, and the ability to coordinate multiple activities are important to success in this role. A high school diploma or GED is required; associate's degree is preferred. Administrative support experience is preferred. Candidates should demonstrate proficiency with Microsoft Office and Microsoft Excel, along with the ability to use standard office equipment. Wilkes University is an independent, comprehensive university dedicated to academic excellence in the liberal arts, sciences, and selected professional programs. The University has approximately 2,000 students at the undergraduate level and over 1,500 full time equivalent students at the graduate and first professional levels. Its institutional focus is on developing strong mentoring relationships with each of its students and contributing vitally to economic development of Northeastern Pennsylvania. The University is located in Wilkes-Barre, Pennsylvania, a revitalized city that is located on the lovely Susquehanna River and is within two and one-half hours driving distance of New York City and Philadelphia. To apply, visit https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/ . Please be sure to include a cover letter, resume or curriculum vitae and three references. Wilkes University is constantly seeking to become a more diverse community and to enhance its capacity to value and capitalize on the cultural richness that diversity brings. The University strongly encourages applications from persons with diverse backgrounds. Wilkes University does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs or activities on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, age, religion, disability, pregnancy, sex/gender, gender identity and/or expression, sexual orientation, marital or family status, military or veteran status, or genetic information. Employment at Wilkes is contingent upon the results of a thorough background screening. PA Act 153 requires that persons working in positions with regular and unsupervised contact with minors complete additional clearances, including FBI fingerprinting and PA criminal and child abuse clearances."
    },
    "https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/4241269": {
      "title": "Plumber",
      "description": "Plumber. Wilkes University. Wilkes University invites applicants for a Plumber in the office of Campus Support Services. This position offers competitive a starting hourly rate and generous benefits package, including paid time off and employee, spouse and dependent tuition benefits. The successful candidate is responsible for working independently, as well as with colleagues, in performing major and minor plumbing repairs throughout campus. This position is responsible for installing, modifying, maintaining, repairing and replacing plumbing systems and equipment. Candidates should have working knowledge of plumbing tools, equipment, materials, systems, methods and practices of proper storage and use of plumbing supplies and related materials, as well as with associated hazards and safety precautions. The successful candidate will perform routine/preventative maintenance to include operating, cleaning, inspecting, troubleshooting, adjusting, tightening and other tasks on all plumbing systems and equipment. They will respond to and prioritizes requests related to plumbing repair, maintenance, modifications and installations. Planning and organizing routine and non-routine work to ensure all projects and tasks are complete as scheduled is key. The Lead Plumber will manage the on-call schedule and delegate calls to other staff members as necessary. Minimum of three (3) years plumbing experience and Journeyman plumbing license required. A valid driver's license and driving record is also required. Applicants should have a high school diploma or G.E.D., certificate and completion of a vocational or trade school program, or any combination of experience and training which provides the knowledge, skills and abilities for successful performance in this position. To apply, visit https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/. Please be sure to include a cover letter, resume or curriculum vitae, and three references. Wilkes University is constantly seeking to become a more diverse community and to enhance its capacity to value and capitalize on the cultural richness that diversity brings. The University strongly encourages applications from persons with diverse backgrounds. Wilkes University does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs or activities on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, age, religion, disability, pregnancy, sex/gender, gender identity and/or expression, sexual orientation, marital or family status, military or veteran status, or genetic information."
    },
    "https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/4249884": {
      "title": "Public Safety Officer",
      "description": "Public Safety Officer. Wilkes University. Wilkes University invites applications for the full-time position of Public Safety Officer. The Public Safety Officer provides security for all University properties. The Public Safety Officer provides security functions via interior and exterior patrol operations; customer service response to University community members; enforces all parking regulations within University parking lots; provides escorts (walking or vehicle) within a reasonable distance of campus. The ideal candidate will be and/or have: Act 235 certified in the State of Pennsylvania within 3 months of hire A high school diploma or G.E.D. equivalent A valid Driver's License Eligible for C.P.R /A.E.D. Certification within 6 months of hire One to three years of credible experience in a similar position or work environment Basic computer skills Professional oral and written communication skills Information on the Wilkes University Annual Security & Fire Safety Report may be viewed at: https://www.wilkes.edu/campus-life/safety-security/annual-security-and-fire-safety-report.aspx To apply, visit https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/ . Please be sure to include a cover letter, resume or curriculum vitae and three references. Wilkes University is constantly seeking to become a more diverse community and to enhance its capacity to value and capitalize on the cultural richness that diversity brings. The University strongly encourages applications from persons with diverse backgrounds. Wilkes University does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs or activities on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, age, religion, disability, pregnancy, sex/gender, gender identity and/or expression, sexual orientation, marital or family status, military or veteran status, or genetic information."
    },
    "https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/4248984": {
      "title": "Public Safety Officer (part-time)",
      "description": "Public Safety Officer (part-time). Wilkes University. Wilkes University invites applications for the part-time position of Public Safety Officer. The Public Safety Officer provides security for all University properties. The Public Safety Officer provides security functions via interior and exterior patrol operations; customer service response to University community members; enforces all parking regulations within University parking lots; provides escorts (walking or vehicle) within a reasonable distance of campus. The ideal candidate will be and/or have: Act 235 certified in the State of Pennsylvania within 3 months of hire A high school diploma or G.E.D. equivalent A valid Driver's License Eligible for C.P.R /A.E.D. Certification within 6 months of hire One to three years of credible experience in a similar position or work environment Basic computer skills Professional oral and written communication skills Information on the Wilkes University Annual Security & Fire Safety Report may be viewed at: https://www.wilkes.edu/campus-life/safety-security/annual-security-and-fire-safety-report.aspx Please be sure to include a cover letter, resume or curriculum vitae and three references. Wilkes University is constantly seeking to become a more diverse community and to enhance its capacity to value and capitalize on the cultural richness that diversity brings. The University strongly encourages applications from persons with diverse backgrounds. Wilkes University does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs or activities on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, age, religion, disability, pregnancy, sex/gender, gender identity and/or expression, sexual orientation, marital or family status, military or veteran status, or genetic information. Employment at Wilkes is contingent upon the results of a thorough background screening. PA Act 153 requires that persons working in positions with regular and unsupervised contact with minors complete additional clearances, including FBI fingerprinting and PA criminal and child abuse clearances."
    },
    "https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/4254989": {
      "title": "Payroll Manager",
      "description": "Payroll Manager. Wilkes University. Wilkes University invites applications for a Payroll Manager to lead the University's payroll operations with full ownership and accountability for accurate, timely, and compliant payroll for faculty, staff, and student employees. This hands-on management role requires a proactive leader who takes responsibility for the entire payroll process and ensures issues are resolved through completion. The Payroll Manager oversees biweekly payroll processing, tax reporting, payroll systems, and regulatory compliance while establishing effective controls, improving procedures, and providing staff training and cross-training as needed. Working closely with Human Resources, Finance, Information Technology, and other campus partners, the manager ensures employee changes, compensation arrangements, and deductions are processed correctly and consistently. The position also evaluates and recommends enhancements to the payroll/HRIS to maximize system capabilities, streamline workflows, and improve operational efficiency. The successful candidate will understand the relationship between payroll and human resources practices and bring a collaborative, team-oriented approach to the role. Exceptional customer service, a positive attitude, and clear, respectful communication are essential. Given access to sensitive personal information and frequent interaction with diverse constituents, this individual must demonstrate the highest regard for confidentiality and maintain professionalism, discretion, and diplomacy at all times. Strong management, organizational, recordkeeping, prioritization, and problem-solving skills, along with accuracy and attention to detail, are critical to success. A bachelor's degree in Accounting, Finance, Business Administration, Human Resources, or a related field and at least five years of progressive payroll experience are required. Candidates must possess extensive knowledge of payroll laws, tax requirements, and wage and hour regulations; advanced Microsoft Excel skills; and the ability to lead and develop staff. Extensive experience and technical knowledge in administering and programming payroll/HRIS systems are essential, with specific Banner experience preferred. Relevant experience includes higher education payroll administration and knowledge of faculty contracts, adjunct compensation, and student employment regulations. Wilkes University is an independent, comprehensive university dedicated to academic excellence in the liberal arts, sciences, and selected professional programs. The University has approximately 2,000 students at the undergraduate level and over 1,500 full time equivalent students at the graduate and first professional levels. Its institutional focus is on developing strong mentoring relationships with each of its students and contributing vitally to economic development of Northeastern Pennsylvania. The University is located in Wilkes-Barre, Pennsylvania, a revitalized city that is located on the lovely Susquehanna River and is within two and one-half hours driving distance of New York City and Philadelphia. Please be sure to include a cover letter, resume or curriculum vitae and three references. Wilkes University is constantly seeking to become a more diverse community and to enhance its capacity to value and capitalize on the cultural richness that diversity brings. The University strongly encourages applications from persons with diverse backgrounds. Wilkes University does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs or activities on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, age, religion, disability, pregnancy, sex/gender, gender identity and/or expression, sexual orientation, marital or family status, military or veteran status, or genetic information. Employment at Wilkes is contingent upon the results of a thorough background screening. PA Act 153 requires that persons working in positions with regular and unsupervised contact with minors complete additional clearances, including FBI fingerprinting and PA criminal and child abuse clearances."
    },
    "https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/4259768": {
      "title": "Carpenter/General Maintenance Technician",
      "description": "Carpenter/General Maintenance Technician. Wilkes University. Wilkes University invites applicants for a Carpenter in the Facilities Department (Monday through Friday 8:00am to 4:30pm). The successful candidate is responsible for working independently, as well as with colleagues, in performing major and minor carpentry repairs throughout campus. Candidate will respond to requests for services, while also performing routine and preventative maintenance on doors, partitions, locks and door hardware, windows and window treatments, flooring, roofs, and roof systems, room furnishings and other items and systems. Maintains, constructs and performs repairs, renovations, alterations and installations on a wide variety of building materials throughout the university. A high school diploma or GED and a valid driver's license is required. The ideal candidate will have a minimum of 5 years prior experience in all aspects of the carpentry field. A practical knowledge of various trades including electrical, plumbing, and painting is preferred. The candidate is required to have proficient technical skills to perform associated tasks, the ability to lift 50lbs and to read and comprehend safety regulations and other documentation pertinent to the position. Basic knowledge of computers (Word, Excel and web based applications) strongly preferred. Candidates must successfully pass a background check. Salary is commensurate with qualifications and experience. Please be sure to include a cover letter, resume or curriculum vitae and three references. Wilkes University is constantly seeking to become a more diverse community and to enhance its capacity to value and capitalize on the cultural richness that diversity brings. The University strongly encourages applications from persons with diverse backgrounds. Wilkes University does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs or activities on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, age, religion, disability, pregnancy, sex/gender, gender identity and/or expression, sexual orientation, marital or family status, military or veteran status, or genetic information. Employment at Wilkes is contingent upon the results of a thorough background screening. PA Act 153 requires that persons working in positions with regular and unsupervised contact with minors complete additional clearances, including FBI fingerprinting and PA criminal and child abuse clearances."
    },
    "https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/4259713": {
      "title": "Faculty of Practice/Speech and Debate Director",
      "description": "Faculty of Practice/Speech and Debate Director. Wilkes University. Wilkes University invites applicants for a Faculty of Practice/Speech and Debate Director in the Communication and Media Studies Department. The high-profile Communication and Media Studies program offers concentrations in public relations and public communication, media and documentary production, news and sports reporting and media and cultural studies. The department enjoys a state-of-the-art media and communication center opened in 2017. The successful candidate is responsible for teaching 21 credits of Public Speaking per academic year and directing the speech/debate program. Position requires coaching and sustaining an active and growing speech/debate program, recruiting students, traveling and coordinating a full tournament schedule, administering annual budget, coordinating intercollegiate tournaments, and assisting the department chair in the coordination of Public Speaking sections. Wilkes has active Pi Kappa Delta and CFA affiliations. A Master's degree and two years coaching experience minimally required. ABD or Ph.D. preferred. Wilkes is AA/EEO employer. Wilkes University is an independent, comprehensive university dedicated to academic excellence in the liberal arts, sciences, and selected professional programs. The University has approximately 2,000 students at the undergraduate level and over 1,500 full time equivalent students at the graduate and first professional levels. Its institutional focus is on developing strong mentoring relationships with each of its students and contributing vitally to economic development of Northeastern Pennsylvania. The University is located in Wilkes-Barre, Pennsylvania, a revitalized city that is located on the lovely Susquehanna River and is within two and one-half hours driving distance of New York City and Philadelphia. To apply, visit https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/. Please be sure to include a cover letter, resume or curriculum vitae and contact information for three references. Questions regarding this position should be sent to Dr. Evene Estwick at evene.estwick@wilkes.edu. Wilkes University is constantly seeking to become a more diverse community and to enhance its capacity to value and capitalize on the cultural richness that diversity brings. The University strongly encourages applications from persons with diverse backgrounds. Wilkes University does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs or activities on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, age, religion, disability, pregnancy, sex/gender, gender identity and/or expression, sexual orientation, marital or family status, military or veteran status, or genetic information. Employment at Wilkes is contingent upon the results of a thorough background screening. PA Act 153 requires that persons working in positions with regular and unsupervised contact with minors complete additional clearances, including FBI fingerprinting and PA criminal and child abuse clearances."
    },
    "https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/4262956": {
      "title": "Adjunct Instructor, Personal and Professional Development",
      "description": "Adjunct Instructor, Personal and Professional Development. Wilkes University. Wilkes University invites applicants for an adjunct instructor in the The Jay S. Sidhu School of Business and Leadership. The Sidhu School is accredited by AACSB. The successful candidate is responsible for teaching four classes of PPD 201 (1 credit course) Personal and Professional Development sections A, B, C, for the Spring 2027 semester. Courses are Wednesday at 12:00, 1:00, and 2:00 from January 20-April 28. A Master's Degree or Higher in Business, Communications or a related field is required. The ideal candidate will have prior experience teaching or training in the areas of self-awareness, emotional intelligence, leadership and leadership style, group dynamics, etc. Salary is commensurate with qualifications and experience. About Wilkes University Wilkes University is an independent, comprehensive university dedicated to academic excellence in the liberal arts, sciences, and selected professional programs. The University has approximately 2,000 students at the undergraduate level and over 1,500 full time equivalent students at the graduate and first professional levels. Its institutional focus is on developing strong mentoring relationships with each of its students and contributing vitally to economic development of Northeastern Pennsylvania. The University is located in Wilkes-Barre, Pennsylvania, a revitalized city that is located on the lovely Susquehanna River and is within two and one-half hours driving distance of New York City and Philadelphia. Application Information To apply, visit Wilkes University Careers . Please be sure to include a cover letter, resume or curriculum vitae and three references. Equal Opportunity Statement Wilkes University is constantly seeking to become a more diverse community and to enhance its capacity to value and capitalize on the cultural richness that diversity brings. The University strongly encourages applications from persons with diverse backgrounds. Wilkes University does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs or activities on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, age, religion, disability, pregnancy, sex/gender, gender identity and/or expression, sexual orientation, marital or family status, military or veteran status, or genetic information."
    },
    "https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/4264182": {
      "title": "Custodial Services Supervisor",
      "description": "Custodial Services Supervisor. Wilkes University. Wilkes University invites applicants for a Night Shift Custodial Supervisor position (Monday through Friday 10:00pm to 6:30am) in the Custodial & Grounds Department. Applicant must be fully committed to providing quality service to our students, faculty and staff. The successful candidate will be a dependable and experienced Custodial Supervisor. They will lead and oversee custodial operations during the evening/night shift. The supervisor will ensure that assigned facilities are clean, safe, sanitary, and properly maintained while providing direction and support to custodial staff. They will inspect areas on a regular basis to make sure all buildings are maintained; respond to, investigate, and triage emergency calls to ensure a timely response. A High School Diploma and equivalent work experience required. Supervisory experience and a minimum of three (3) years prior experience in a similar work environment are required. A demonstrated ability to handle custodial equipment as well as knowledge of best practices in custodial care and procedures will be essential to success. The candidate must have the ability to provide supervision, multitask and assist with technical issues and contingencies. This is a working supervisor position, so knowledge and ability to perform custodial tasks and train staff will be critical. Must possess strong communication and interpersonal skills and be able to prioritize projects and gather information. Strong working knowledge of computers (Word, Excel, database applications, email and internet applications) required. Strong project management skills required. Ability to lift at least 50lbs. and to read and comprehend safety regulations and other documentation pertinent to the position. Salary is commensurate with qualifications and experience. Wilkes University is an independent, comprehensive university dedicated to academic excellence in the liberal arts, sciences, and selected professional programs. The University has approximately 2,000 students at the undergraduate level and over 1,500 full time equivalent students at the graduate and first professional levels. Its institutional focus is on developing strong mentoring relationships with each of its students and contributing vitally to economic development of Northeastern Pennsylvania. The University is located in Wilkes-Barre, Pennsylvania, a revitalized city that is located on the lovely Susquehanna River and is within two and one-half hours driving distance of New York City and Philadelphia. To apply, visit https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/ . Please be sure to include a cover letter, resume or curriculum vitae and three references. Wilkes University is constantly seeking to become a more diverse community and to enhance its capacity to value and capitalize on the cultural richness that diversity brings. The University strongly encourages applications from persons with diverse backgrounds. Wilkes University does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs or activities on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, age, religion, disability, pregnancy, sex/gender, gender identity and/or expression, sexual orientation, marital or family status, military or veteran status, or genetic information. Employment at Wilkes is contingent upon the results of a thorough background screening. PA Act 153 requires that persons working in positions with regular and unsupervised contact with minors complete additional clearances, including FBI fingerprinting and PA criminal and child abuse clearances."
    },
    "https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/4267719": {
      "title": "Custodian (Day Shift Refresh)",
      "description": "Custodian (Day Shift Refresh). Wilkes University. Wilkes University invites applicants for a part-time day shift Refresh Custodial Worker in the Campus Support Services department. This role operates with a high degree of scheduling flexibility working up to 20 hours per week within the Monday-Friday 9 am to 5 pm work week. The position requires: Strong communication skills: Outgoing, friendly, and comfortable communicating professionally with customers and other team members. High attention to detail: Pride in keeping a public-facing space immaculate. Independence & Professionalism: Ability to stay on task and manage your time while working around office staff and visitors with minimal disruption. The successful candidate must be able to work independently and is responsible for daily cleaning of restrooms, classrooms, hallways and office areas in campus facilities including residence halls, athletic areas, administrative and academic buildings. The Custodian will provide cleaning and sanitation services in addition to the use of light floor machines and attachments (e.g., vacuums, floor buffers, carpet extractors, etc.), perform general maintenance work (e.g., replace light bulbs, plunge toilets, etc.), assist with event set-ups and seasonal grounds maintenance as well as removal and transportation of garbage and recyclables from throughout campus. A high school diploma or GED and a valid PA driver's license are required. The ideal candidate is required to have proficient technical skills to perform associated tasks, the ability to lift 40 lbs. and the ability to read and comprehend safety regulations and other documentation pertinent to the position. Basic knowledge of computers (Word, Excel and web-based applications) strongly preferred. Candidates must successfully pass a background check. Wilkes University is an independent, comprehensive university dedicated to academic excellence in the liberal arts, sciences, and selected professional programs. The University has approximately 2,000 students at the undergraduate level and over 1,500 full time equivalent students at the graduate and first professional levels. Its institutional focus is on developing strong mentoring relationships with each of its students and contributing vitally to economic development of Northeastern Pennsylvania. The University is located in Wilkes-Barre, Pennsylvania, a revitalized city that is located on the lovely Susquehanna River and is within two and one-half hours driving distance of New York City and Philadelphia. To apply, visit https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/ . Please be sure to include a cover letter, resume or curriculum vitae and three references. Wilkes University is constantly seeking to become a more diverse community and to enhance its capacity to value and capitalize on the cultural richness that diversity brings. The University strongly encourages applications from persons with diverse backgrounds. Wilkes University does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs or activities on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, age, religion, disability, pregnancy, sex/gender, gender identity and/or expression, sexual orientation, marital or family status, military or veteran status, or genetic information. Employment at Wilkes is contingent upon the results of a thorough background screening. PA Act 153 requires that persons working in positions with regular and unsupervised contact with minors complete additional clearances, including FBI fingerprinting and PA criminal and child abuse clearances."
    },
    "https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/4268617": {
      "title": "Director of Professional Development and External Engagement",
      "description": "Director of Professional Development and External Engagement. Wilkes University. Wilkes University invites applications for a Director of Professional Development and External Engagement in the Sidhu School of Business and Leadership. This full-time, 12-month position leads initiatives that strengthen students' career readiness, leadership development, and connections with employers, alumni, and the business community. The Director oversees the Personal and Professional Development (PPD) program, including curriculum development, instructional quality, assessment, and continuous improvement, and teaches up to six credits of PPD courses per semester. The position also provides individual career guidance to seniors and develops innovative programs and events that connect students with industry leaders and professional opportunities. A central responsibility is cultivating corporate and community partnerships that support internships, employment opportunities, financial support, and meaningful student engagement. The Director coordinates the College of Business and Engineering Dean's Executive Advisory Board and Student Advisory Board programs, collaborates with campus partners, tracks graduate and alumni employment outcomes, and contributes to strategic planning and AACSB accreditation efforts. A master's degree in business administration or a related field is required. Candidates should bring experience in curriculum development, professional development programming, program assessment, and strategic partnership building, along with knowledge of workforce trends, employer recruitment practices, and experiential education. Strong communication, relationship-building, organizational, analytical, and fiscal planning skills are essential. Understanding of business school accreditation processes, preferably AACSB, and the ability to lead collaborative, data-informed initiatives are also highly preferred. Wilkes University is an independent, comprehensive university dedicated to academic excellence in the liberal arts, sciences, and selected professional programs. The University has approximately 2,000 students at the undergraduate level and over 1,500 full time equivalent students at the graduate and first professional levels. Its institutional focus is on developing strong mentoring relationships with each of its students and contributing vitally to economic development of Northeastern Pennsylvania. The University is located in Wilkes-Barre, Pennsylvania, a revitalized city that is located on the lovely Susquehanna River and is within two and one-half hours driving distance of New York City and Philadelphia. To apply, visit Wilkes University Careers . Please be sure to include a cover letter, resume or curriculum vitae and three references. Wilkes University is constantly seeking to become a more diverse community and to enhance its capacity to value and capitalize on the cultural richness that diversity brings. The University strongly encourages applications from persons with diverse backgrounds. Wilkes University does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs or activities on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, age, religion, disability, pregnancy, sex/gender, gender identity and/or expression, sexual orientation, marital or family status, military or veteran status, or genetic information. Employment at Wilkes is contingent upon the results of a thorough background screening. PA Act 153 requires that persons working in positions with regular and unsupervised contact with minors complete additional clearances, including FBI fingerprinting and PA criminal and child abuse clearances."
    },
    "https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/4266567": {
      "title": "Print and Mail Delivery Associate",
      "description": "Print and Mail Delivery Associate. Wilkes University. Wilkes University invites applications for a Print & Mail Delivery Associate to support campus mail, package delivery, and print services. Reporting to the Print & Mail Services Manager, this position helps ensure efficient daily operations while providing courteous, dependable service to students, faculty, and staff. The work schedule is Monday through Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. Primary responsibilities include collecting, sorting, and delivering incoming and interoffice mail, packages, and print shop orders; preparing and processing outgoing shipments; operating mailing equipment; and maintaining delivery records and mailbox information. The Associate drives University delivery vehicles, responds to postal inquiries, and provides backup support for shipping, receiving, and print shop functions. A high school diploma or GED, a valid Pennsylvania driver's license, and at least one year of related clerical, records management, mailroom, or shipping and receiving experience are required. Candidates must demonstrate strong customer service, communication, organizational, and time-management skills; proficiency in Microsoft Word, Excel, and Outlook; and the ability to work effectively with a diverse campus community. Campus mailroom experience and familiarity with postal equipment and regulations are preferred. This position requires regular in-person attendance, extended periods of walking and standing, and the ability to lift and move packages up to 50 pounds regularly and up to 100 pounds occasionally. Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform essential functions. About Wilkes University Wilkes University is an independent, comprehensive university dedicated to academic excellence in the liberal arts, sciences, and selected professional programs. The University has approximately 2,000 students at the undergraduate level and over 1,500 full time equivalent students at the graduate and first professional levels. Its institutional focus is on developing strong mentoring relationships with each of its students and contributing vitally to economic development of Northeastern Pennsylvania. The University is located in Wilkes-Barre, Pennsylvania, a revitalized city that is located on the lovely Susquehanna River and is within two and one-half hours driving distance of New York City and Philadelphia. Application Information To apply, visit Wilkes University Careers . Please be sure to include a cover letter, resume or curriculum vitae and three references. Equal Opportunity Statement Wilkes University is constantly seeking to become a more diverse community and to enhance its capacity to value and capitalize on the cultural richness that diversity brings. The University strongly encourages applications from persons with diverse backgrounds. Wilkes University does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs or activities on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, age, religion, disability, pregnancy, sex/gender, gender identity and/or expression, sexual orientation, marital or family status, military or veteran status, or genetic information. Employment at Wilkes is contingent upon the results of a thorough background screening. PA Act 153 requires that persons working in positions with regular and unsupervised contact with minors complete additional clearances, including FBI fingerprinting and PA criminal and child abuse clearances."
    },
    "https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/4269418": {
      "title": "Coordinator of Enrollment and Student Success",
      "description": "Coordinator of Enrollment and Student Success. Wilkes University. Wilkes University invites applicants to apply for the Coordinator of Enrollment and Student Success position in the Nesbitt School of Pharmacy (NSoP) . The NSoP's mission is \"To educate and develop highly qualified professionals and notably contribute to the ever-changing science and practice of pharmacy.\" This position will directly support this mission by assisting with recruiting a highly qualified applicant pool and supporting student success initiatives. The NSoP is fully accredited by the Accreditation Council for Pharmacy Education (ACPE). The successful candidate will work as part of the NSoP enrollment and student success team to successfully execute recruitment events, admissions, and student success initiatives within the NSoP. Key responsibilities include: Effectively represent the NSoP to candidates for the Pre-Pharmacy Guaranteed Seat (PPGS) and Doctor of Pharmacy (Pharm.D.) programs. Assist with recruitment, enrollment, and marketing activities for the PPGS and Pharm.D. programs. Collaborate with other departments, including Marketing Communications, Admissions and Financial Aid and the Office of the Registrar. Collect, organize and maintain academic and non-academic data. Prepare, distribute, and collect enrollment and academic documentation, including academic status records, admission letters, applications, contracts, and transcripts. Report data to contribute to required ACPE accreditation surveys and reports on pharmacy education standards. Lead PPGS and Pharm.D. applicants through the matriculation process into the professional program. Work directly with student pharmacists and serve in an advisory role including supporting student development through transitions into the Pharm.D. program, personal transitions, those experiencing academic difficulty or on academic support plans. Provide leadership through selection, training and support of First-Year Student Pharmacist Peer Mentors. Contribute to programs that promote engagement and a sense of belonging. Create and/or distribute resources to support student success. Monitor key metrics that assess student success, well-being, and belonging. Plan and coordinate logistics of NSoP sponsored events (e.g. Hooding Ceremony, White Coat Ceremony, professional interviews, orientations, and camps). Manage the budget related to scholarships, enrollment and student success sponsored events. Provide executive administrative support for the Associate Dean of Enrollment and Student Success. The successful candidate will report to the Associate Dean of Enrollment and Student Success in the NSoP. This is a full-time, twelve-month position. A bachelor's degree and minimum three years of professional work experience is required. Experience in higher education is preferred. The ideal candidate should be organized, with an ability to prioritize multiple high priority tasks, meet project deadlines with attention to detail and accuracy, work independently on assigned tasks, contribute as an effective team member, and should possess excellent communication skills. The candidate should possess the ability to handle confidential information with discretion and professionalism. Strong critical thinking (interpretation and application of information and problem solving) skills are necessary. The ideal candidate should be proficient with technology and easily able to adapt to learning new programs. Flexibility to work occasional evenings and weekends is expected. Occasional travel to recruitment events hosted off campus is required. A valid driver's license, access to an automobile and safe driving practices are required. Travel expenses for approved business-related travel are provided but must have reliable means of transportation. Salary is commensurate with qualifications and experience. Wilkes University is an independent, comprehensive university dedicated to academic excellence in the liberal arts, sciences, and selected professional programs. The University has approximately 2,000 students at the undergraduate level and over 1,500 full time equivalent students at the graduate and first professional levels. Its institutional focus is on developing strong mentoring relationships with each of its students and contributing vitally to economic development of Northeastern Pennsylvania. The University is located in Wilkes-Barre, Pennsylvania, a revitalized city that is located on the lovely Susquehanna River and is within two and one-half hours driving distance of New York City and Philadelphia. To apply, visit https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/ . Please be sure to include a cover letter, resume or curriculum vitae and three references. Wilkes University is constantly seeking to become a more diverse community and to enhance its capacity to value and capitalize on the cultural richness that diversity brings. The University strongly encourages applications from persons with diverse backgrounds. Wilkes University does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs or activities on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, age, religion, disability, pregnancy, sex/gender, gender identity and/or expression, sexual orientation, marital or family status, military or veteran status, or genetic information. Employment at Wilkes is contingent upon the results of a thorough background screening. PA Act 153 requires that persons working in positions with regular and unsupervised contact with minors complete additional clearances, including FBI fingerprinting and PA criminal and child abuse clearances."
    },
    "https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/4273056": {
      "title": "Dean, College of Business and Engineering",
      "description": "Dean, College of Business and Engineering. Wilkes University. Wilkes University invites applicants for the next Dean of the College of Business and Engineering. Reporting to the Provost and Senior Vice President for Academic Affairs, the Dean serves as the College's chief academic, administrative, and fiscal officer, providing strategic leadership for the Jay S. Sidhu School of Business and Leadership, the School of Engineering, and the Department of Aerospace Studies. This full-time, 12-month administrative appointment carries faculty rank, with an anticipated start date of July 2027. The Dean will foster a unified, collaborative college culture while respecting the distinct strengths and accreditation requirements of business and engineering. Major responsibilities include advancing academic quality and interdisciplinary programs; maintaining AACSB and ABET accreditation; recruiting, mentoring, and supporting faculty and staff; overseeing budgets and resources; and strengthening enrollment, student success, and experiential learning. The Dean will also lead fundraising and cultivate alumni, industry, and community partnerships that expand opportunities for students, support research and innovation, and contribute to regional economic development. Candidates must hold an earned doctorate in business, engineering, or a closely related field from an accredited institution and demonstrate a record of teaching, scholarship, and service that merits appointment as a tenured full professor in a College department. At least five years of progressively responsible academic leadership, direct experience with AACSB or ABET accreditation reviews and self-studies, and experience managing budgets, personnel, and strategic planning in higher education are required. The successful candidate will bring a collaborative, transparent leadership style; excellent communication and relationship-building skills; sound judgment; and a commitment to student success, faculty development, and an inclusive learning environment. Preferred qualifications include multidisciplinary leadership, experience with both AACSB and ABET, and demonstrated success in fundraising, external partnerships, interdisciplinary program development, and enrollment growth. About Wilkes University Wilkes University is an independent, comprehensive university dedicated to academic excellence in the liberal arts, sciences, and selected professional programs. The University has approximately 2,000 students at the undergraduate level and over 1,500 full time equivalent students at the graduate and first professional levels. Its institutional focus is on developing strong mentoring relationships with each of its students and contributing vitally to economic development of Northeastern Pennsylvania. The University is located in Wilkes-Barre, Pennsylvania, a revitalized city that is located on the lovely Susquehanna River and is within two and one-half hours driving distance of New York City and Philadelphia. Application Information To apply, visit Wilkes University Careers . Please be sure to include a cover letter, resume or curriculum vitae and three references. Equal Opportunity Statement Wilkes University is constantly seeking to become a more diverse community and to enhance its capacity to value and capitalize on the cultural richness that diversity brings. The University strongly encourages applications from persons with diverse backgrounds. Wilkes University does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs or activities on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, age, religion, disability, pregnancy, sex/gender, gender identity and/or expression, sexual orientation, marital or family status, military or veteran status, or genetic information. Employment at Wilkes is contingent upon the results of a thorough background screening. PA Act 153 requires that persons working in positions with regular and unsupervised contact with minors complete additional clearances, including FBI fingerprinting and PA criminal and child abuse clearances."
    },
    "https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/4272568": {
      "title": "Internship Coordinator",
      "description": "Internship Coordinator. Wilkes University. Wilkes University invites applicants for the Internship Coordinator in the Center for Career Development and Internships (CCDI). Developing and managing internship opportunities for students and coordinating internship placement are two main objectives of this position. The ideal candidate will counsel students on the value of internships as they relate to career development and will help students with preparation for these experiences. Creating strategies to promote internship value on campus and externally will be key. The Internship Coordinator will also develop and maintain relationships with employers and sites to continue placing Wilkes University student interns in meaningful experiential learning environments. The ideal candidate should be organized, be able to work independently while also understanding how to be coachable, contribute to the CCDI team, and possess excellent communication skills. The ideal candidate should be proficient with technology and easily able to learn new programs. Flexibility to work occasional evenings and weekends is required. A valid driver's license and access to an automobile are expected. A bachelor's degree in Communications, Business Administration, Education or a related field is required and 1-3 years of experience in higher education is preferred. Wilkes University is an independent, comprehensive university dedicated to academic excellence in the liberal arts, sciences, and selected professional programs. The University has approximately 2,000 undergraduate students and over 1,500 full-time equivalent students at the graduate and first professional levels. Its institutional focus is on developing strong mentoring relationships with each of its students and contributing vitally to economic development of Northeastern Pennsylvania. The University is located in Wilkes-Barre, Pennsylvania, a revitalized city, located on the scenic Susquehanna River, that provides an affordable cost of living and is within two and one-half hours driving distance of New York City and Philadelphia. To apply, visit https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/. Please be sure to include a cover letter, resume and three references. Wilkes University is constantly seeking to become a more diverse community and to enhance its capacity to value and capitalize on the cultural richness that diversity brings. The University strongly encourages applications from persons with diverse backgrounds. Wilkes University does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs or activities on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, age, religion, disability, pregnancy, sex/gender, gender identity and/or expression, sexual orientation, marital or family status, military or veteran status, or genetic information."
    },
    "https://wilkesuniversitycareers.applicantpro.com/jobs/4274097": {
      "title": "Dean, College of Health and Education",
      "description": "Dean, College of Health and Education. Wilkes University. Wilkes University invites applications for Dean of the College of Health and Education. Reporting to the Provost and Senior Vice President for Academic Affairs, the Dean serves as the College's chief academic, administrative, and fiscal officer, providing strategic leadership for the Passan School of Nursing, the Nesbitt School of Pharmacy, and the Dr. Richard Abas Alley School of Education. This full-time, 12-month administrative appointment carries faculty rank, with an anticipated start date of July 2027. The Dean will foster a collaborative, inclusive college culture while respecting each school's distinct identity and professional requirements. Major responsibilities include advancing academic quality and program development; maintaining disciplinary accreditations and state authorizations; recruiting, mentoring, and supporting faculty and staff; managing budgets and resources; and strengthening enrollment, retention, and student success. The Dean will also lead College fundraising efforts and cultivate clinical, school district, alumni, and community partnerships that support student placements, experiential learning, and professional preparation. Candidates must hold an earned doctorate or other appropriate degree in nursing, education, pharmacy, or a closely related field from an accredited institution and demonstrate a record of teaching, scholarship, and service that merits appointment as a tenured full professor in a College department. At least five years of progressively responsible academic leadership, direct experience with accreditation reviews and self-studies, and experience managing budgets, personnel, and strategic planning in higher education are required. The successful candidate will bring a collaborative, transparent leadership style; excellent communication, interpersonal, and conflict-resolution skills; sound judgment; and a commitment to student success, faculty development, and an inclusive learning environment. Preferred qualifications include multidisciplinary leadership, experience with nursing, pharmacy, and/or education accreditation, and demonstrated success in fundraising, external partnerships, grant-funded initiatives, and enrollment growth. About Wilkes University Wilkes University is an independent, comprehensive university dedicated to academic excellence in the liberal arts, sciences, and selected professional programs. The University has approximately 2,000 students at the undergraduate level and over 1,500 full time equivalent students at the graduate and first professional levels. Its institutional focus is on developing strong mentoring relationships with each of its students and contributing vitally to economic development of Northeastern Pennsylvania. The University is located in Wilkes-Barre, Pennsylvania, a revitalized city that is located on the lovely Susquehanna River and is within two and one-half hours driving distance of New York City and Philadelphia. Application Information To apply, visit Wilkes University Careers . Please be sure to include a cover letter, resume or curriculum vitae and three references. Equal Opportunity Statement Wilkes University is constantly seeking to become a more diverse community and to enhance its capacity to value and capitalize on the cultural richness that diversity brings. The University strongly encourages applications from persons with diverse backgrounds. Wilkes University does not discriminate in its employment practices or in its educational programs or activities on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, age, religion, disability, pregnancy, sex/gender, gender identity and/or expression, sexual orientation, marital or family status, military or veteran status, or genetic information."
